{
  "id": "ss.relic.doubleyolk",
  "name": "Double yolk",
  "description": "An egg cracked open and set down, the lower shell a pale cup with a jagged rim, the inside of the far wall showing bone-white behind, and the white filling it lit rather than shadowed. Two orange yolks sit in it side by side, the left one a size bigger than the right, both riding up above the broken rim so the silhouette is a cup with two domes. Elites leave two chests with this relic, and two yolks in one shell is the same luck said with a kitchen. The front rim is drawn after the yolks so they sit in the cup instead of on it; nothing inside is dark, because a dark hollow behind a bright rim is a hole.",
